From 289837c6a048151fe24ab3a96baf179621637baf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:32:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(ui): fix Rules-of-Hooks violation in global
 UnlockCelebration (React #300/#310)

Root cause of both crashes reported from the device (#300 on tapping
'Finish Quiz', then #310 after the post-quiz toast is dismissed on
Home): UnlockCelebration is mounted globally in __root.tsx, so it is
present on every screen. It had an early 'if (isInQuizCelebration)
return null;' placed between its first batch of hooks (useState + 5x
useRef) and two useEffect calls below it.

- The instant finishQuiz() queues a pendingCelebration of type 'full',
  isInQuizCelebration flips to true on this globally-mounted
  component's next render, and it now returns after fewer hooks than
  the render before it -> error #300. This fires right when the user
  taps 'Finish Quiz', which matches exactly what was reported.
- Later, once the Home-screen toast dismisses that pendingCelebration,
  isInQuizCelebration flips back to false, and the component calls
  more hooks than it did on its previous (gated) render -> error #310.
  This matches the second crash reported after killing and reopening
  the app.

This is unrelated to any of the quiz-flow routing fixes in recent
commits; it's a standalone, pre-existing bug that would fire any time
a quiz celebration is queued or dismissed, regardless of which quiz
entry point or completion screen is used.

Fix: keep isInQuizCelebration as a plain boolean used only inside the
two useEffect bodies and the final JSX return (both safe places for
conditionals), so every render calls the exact same hooks in the same
order.
---
 src/components/UnlockCelebration.tsx | 21 +++++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/components/UnlockCelebration.tsx b/src/components/UnlockCelebration.tsx
index 86953b4..bbd0354 100644
--- a/src/components/UnlockCelebration.tsx
+++ b/src/components/UnlockCelebration.tsx
@@ -96,12 +96,15 @@ export function UnlockCelebration() {
   }
 
   // GATE: Suppress unlock celebrations during quiz celebration
-  // If there's a pending "full" celebration (quiz), don't show unlock popups
+  // If there's a pending "full" celebration (quiz), don't show unlock popups.
+  // IMPORTANT: this must stay a plain boolean used *inside* the effects and
+  // the final render below - never an early `return` placed between hook
+  // calls. This component is mounted globally (see __root.tsx), so an early
+  // return here before the two useEffect calls below means it renders with
+  // fewer hooks the instant a quiz celebration is queued (React error #300),
+  // and with more hooks the instant that celebration is dismissed (error
+  // #310). Hooks must run the same number of times on every render.
   const isInQuizCelebration = progress.pendingCelebrations?.some((c) => c.type === "full");
-  if (isInQuizCelebration) {
-    console.log("[UnlockCelebration] Quiz celebration in progress - suppressing unlock popups");
-    return null;
-  }
 
   useEffect(
     () => () => {
@@ -111,6 +114,11 @@ export function UnlockCelebration() {
   );
 
   useEffect(() => {
+    if (isInQuizCelebration) {
+      console.log("[UnlockCelebration] Quiz celebration in progress - suppressing unlock popups");
+      return;
+    }
+
     // GATE: Only show achievement popups AFTER user completes onboarding
     // During onboarding, suppress celebrations to avoid UI noise
     if (!progress.onboarded) {
@@ -244,8 +252,9 @@ export function UnlockCelebration() {
       timerRef.current = null;
       setPieces(null);
     }, 3200);
-  }, [progress]);
+  }, [progress, isInQuizCelebration]);
 
+  if (isInQuizCelebration) return null;
   if (!pieces) return null;
 
   return (
